  "details": "<p>The Villa San Marco at Stabiae was excavated from 1749 to 1754, again in the 1950s, and again in 2011. Restorations were carried out in 2011 and 2012. The villa covers some 11,000 square meters, making it one of the largest Roman residential villas in the Bay of Naples.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Villa San Marco originates in the Augustan period and was subsequently expanded during the reign of Claudius. Its owner may have been a freedman of Claudius.",
